<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.macro.skewaccrual.plist — launchd agent for the daily ThetaData skew-
  accrual producer (MO-PAID-013 W2-2 — A-F03-W2-2).

  WHAT THIS LANE DOES
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Runs ops/launchd/run_skew_accrual.sh daily. The script:
    1. refreshes the dedicated checkout /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt off
       origin/main (refuses on a dirty or stale checkout; never pushes);
    2. gates on the ThetaData EOD store freshness (SPY eod shard >= T-1
       expected NYSE session, 6 x 20 min retries);
    3. runs the W2-1b accrue command to append today's per-underlying skew
       to data/options_skew/snapshots.parquet (canonical-wins source-stamped
       upsert from W2-1b);
    4. verifies the ledger has actually grown under the accrue (BLOCKER-2
       fix — refuses a no-op accrue on a pre-populated bootstrap);
    5. publishes data/options_skew to R2 via the publish_r2 options_skew
       dir. Every publish writes a real manifest (no no-manifest flag) so
       bulk consumers (fetch_r2 / audit_r2) read the freshness anchor.

  This lane is OFF by default — the seat installs the plist per the runbook
  (research/MARKET_ONTOLOGY_F03_SKEW_ACCRUAL_LANE_2026-09-22.md).

  SCHEDULE
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  StartCalendarInterval fires weekdays at 05:30 LOCAL wall-clock. launchd
  has no UTC mode; the runner uses the host's America/Los_Angeles zone
  (mirroring optionsmatrix + thetadata-r2sync). 05:30 local = 13:30Z
  during PST (UTC-8) and 12:30Z during PDT (UTC-7). Both are safely
  AFTER the observed 11:30Z ThetaData EOD refresh on either side of the
  DST switch — the previous 04:30-local choice raced the 11:30Z refresh
  by zero hours during PDT, which is BLOCKER-4 of this packet. The new
  value buys at minimum one hour of headroom year-round.

  The reason the local wall-clock is 05:30 (not 06:30 or 07:30) is that
  the ThetaData EOD refresh observed on the M1 ops host settles around
  11:30Z. Anything later than 05:30 local shrinks the post-refresh
  window without buying anything; anything earlier races it during PDT.
  05:30 is the tightest safe point.

  WEEKDAY SCOPE
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Weekday 1–5 only (Mon–Fri). Weekends skip because NYSE is closed and the
  ThetaData EOD store carries Friday's session across the weekend; running
  the accrual on a weekend would either gate-fail (no new session yet) or
  re-publish Friday's content under a Saturday date.

  ENV FILE / SECRETS
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  R2 credentials, THETADATA_STORE, and THETA_API_KEY are sourced from
  /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/.env via run_with_env.sh. NEVER inline
  secrets in EnvironmentVariables — use the wrapper.

  Required env vars (must be present in the .env):
    R2_ENDPOINT, R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID, R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, R2_BUCKET
    THETADATA_STORE=/Users/chriswong/theta-ops-wt/data/thetadata_eod
    THETA_API_KEY=<vendor credential for live chains>
    GITHUB_TOKEN=<needed for any future gh interaction; not used by the
                  runner today>

  INSTALL (as the mac user who owns the M1 ops host — not root):
    cp ops/launchd/com.macro.skewaccrual.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.macro.skewaccrual.plist

  UNINSTALL:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.macro.skewaccrual.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.macro.skewaccrual.plist

  DO NOT load this plist directly from the repo. Copy first — launchd requires
  the exact plist path when unloading.

  WORKING DIRECTORY:
    /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt  (dedicated lane checkout; NOT flow-ops-wt
    or theta-ops-wt — both are stale/dirty by design and would undermine a
    "checkout is clean" assertion. The dedicated checkout is created by the
    install runbook as a sparse clone carrying engine, scripts, lib, config,
    ops, data/options_skew.)

  SMOKE / DRY-RUN (no R2 publish — accrues locally only):
    set -a
    source /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/.env
    set +a
    SKEW_FRESHNESS_BYPASS=1 SKEW_DRY_RUN=1 \
      "/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/ops/launchd/run_skew_accrual.sh"

  MANUAL RUN (full, with R2 publish — same as nightly launchd):
    set -a
    source /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/.env
    set +a
    SKEW_FRESHNESS_BYPASS=1 \
      "/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/ops/launchd/run_skew_accrual.sh"

  LOG TAILING:
    tail -f /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-state/logs/skewaccrual.stdout.log \
            /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-state/logs/skewaccrual.stderr.log

  All run-state files (logs, receipts, locks, .skew_pre_rows) live under
  /Users/chriswong/skew-ops-state — the SAME sibling state directory the
  runner defaults to ($SKEW_STATE_DIR). launchd paths are literal (no
  env-var expansion), so the destination is hardcoded to the default; if
  the operator overrides $SKEW_STATE_DIR at install time they must update
  StandardOutPath / StandardErrorPath to match. NEVER /tmp/* — the round-1
  /tmp/skewaccrual.*.log pair was inside the disposable /tmp tree but the
  launchd-managed files still outrank the runner's "all run-state files
  live outside $REPO under a sibling state directory" contract, so both
  halves of the contract now point at $SKEW_STATE_DIR.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.macro.skewaccrual</string>

  <!--
    ProgramArguments chain:
      run_with_env.sh  <env_file>  run_skew_accrual.sh
    The wrapper sources the .env file before executing the runner.
    The runner is a shell script (not a Python -m invocation) because it owns
    the freshness-wait retry loop before handing off to Python.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/ops/launchd/run_with_env.sh</string>
    <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/.env</string>
    <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt/ops/launchd/run_skew_accrual.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!--
    WorkingDirectory is the dedicated lane checkout. The runner re-checks-out
    origin/main on every run, so this is also the read-side baseline.
    flow-ops-wt and theta-ops-wt are deliberately NOT used — see install
    runbook for why.
  -->
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt</string>

  <!--
    05:30 LOCAL daily = 13:30Z during PST (UTC-8) / 12:30Z during PDT
    (UTC-7) — at minimum 1 hour after the 11:30Z ThetaData EOD refresh
    observed on the M1 ops host, on either side of the DST switch. Host
    is assumed America/Los_Angeles (consistent with optionsmatrix and
    thetadata-r2sync plists). launchd has no UTC mode; the local time is
    intentionally chosen to be the tightest safe point year-round.
    Weekday 1 to 5 only (NYSE is closed weekends).
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer>
      <key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer>
      <key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer>
      <key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer>
      <key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Hour</key><integer>5</integer>
      <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
    <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-wt</string>
    <!--
      THETADATA_STORE is sourced from .env via run_with_env.sh above.
      Set it here too so the freshness-gate Python snippet can find the store
      even if the .env parse fails for any reason (belt-and-suspenders only;
      the .env value wins because run_with_env.sh exports it first).
    -->
    <key>THETADATA_STORE</key>
    <string>/Users/chriswong/theta-ops-wt/data/thetadata_eod</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-state/logs/skewaccrual.stdout.log</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/chriswong/skew-ops-state/logs/skewaccrual.stderr.log</string>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <false/>

  <!-- Throttle: if the job crashes in under 10s, wait 60s before retrying. -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>60</integer>

  <!--
    Per-session launchd Aqua: skewaccrual runs in the user's GUI session so it
    can write /tmp/* and reach the M1 ops-host network. Aqua is the standard
    for interactive user-session agents (Background would be for system-wide).
  -->
  <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
  <string>Aqua</string>

</dict>
</plist>